.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt ASN1_ITEM_NEW 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ASN1_item_new_ex ,
.Nm ASN1_item_new
.Nd create new ASN.1 values
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/asn1.h
.Ft ASN1_VALUE *
.Fo ASN1_item_new_ex
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft ASN1_VALUE *
.Fo ASN1_item_new
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn ASN1_item_new_ex
creates a new
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
structure based on the
.Sy ASN1_ITEM
template given in the
.Fa it
parameter.
If any algorithm fetches are required during the process then they will
use the
.Vt OSSL_LIB_CTX
provided in the
.Fa libctx
parameter and the property query string in
.Fa propq .
See
.Xr crypto 7
for more information about algorithm fetching.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_item_new
is the same as
.Fn ASN1_item_new_ex
except that the default
.Vt OSSL_LIB_CTX
is used (i.e.
NULL) and with a NULL property query string.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn ASN1_item_new_ex
and
.Fn ASN1_item_new
return a pointer to the newly created
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
or NULL on error.
.Sh HISTORY
The function
.Fn ASN1_item_new_ex
was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
